Hanuman Ansh is a 2026 Hindi biographical devotional drama written and directed by Vishal Chaturvedi. Inspired by the life of the revered Indian saint Neem Karoli Baba (Maharaj-ji), the film traces young Lakshman Narayan Sharma's spiritual journey after losing his mother as he discovers faith through humility, devotion to Lord Hanuman, and selfless service (seva)


Plot & Themes

• The Quest: After his mother passes away, a grieving boy leaves home hoping to find God and reunite with her.
• Spiritual Awakening: Wandering across temples, rivers, and villages in pre-Independence Northern India, he learns that devotion is realized through compassion, feeding the hungry, and silent blessings rather than escaping the world.
• Core Message: The film centers on unconditional love, devotion to Lord Hanuman, and selfless service, carrying a U certificate suitable for family viewing.

Cast & Crew

• Director & Writer: Vishal Chaturvedi
• Producers: Vishal Chaturvedi, Ragini Sona, Namrata G. Singh, and Anupriya A. Nagar
• Key Cast: Shobhinaw Satyaa (Neem Karoli Baba), Vihaan Shedge (young Neem Karoli Baba), Chandan K. Anand, Anil Rastogi, Purnima Tiwari, and Gulshan Pandey
• Runtime: 150 minutes (2 hours 30 minutes)

Release & Reception

• Theatrical Run: Released in India on August 7, 2026, and expanded overseas in September 2026. Despite a quiet opening on a micro-budget of roughly ₹1.7–2 crore, strong word-of-mouth turned it into a major sleeper hit.
• Streaming: Available to stream on SonyLIV.
• Reception: Audiences praised its emotional warmth and sincerity, while critics gave mixed-to-positive reviews—commending its spiritual message and lead performance while noting pacing and VFX limitations.